- Shared mechanisms: Two mechanisms produced the 13 blocking findings. (1) Ownership of an unread token's diagnostics between the validator and the converter: round 1's gram findings 1-4 and undirected findings 1-2, round 2's fix2 finding and undirected2 finding 1, and round 3's undirected3 finding. Round 1's correction replaced the validator's guess (ownedByUnreadReading) with the converter recording the statements it marks as Luau's (Parser.unreadStatements), which removed the second implementation rather than patching instances; the later findings in this class were each one body kind the readers did not yet cover (bracketed alternator arms, a closure read as a chunk, the define method's explicit `function f()` spelling), and the last of them is a one-line ancestor condition. (2) Luau's attribute lexeme emulated in the parser (introduced by round 2's correction to undirected2 finding 2): round 3's fix3 findings 1 and 2 were a zero-width synthetic `end` taken as a glued name and a second token-entry path (interpolations) that skipped the emulation; the fix makes both entries call readAttributeLexemes and excludes zero-width tokens from adjacency. Round 1's gram finding 5 (grammar lookahead justification) stands alone and was fixed by restructuring the rule.
