- Residual risk: 77fcc6ed6 (4 code lines in validateAssignmentValue.ts plus 9 test lines) has had no independent review. The attribute emulation mutates the `@` token's location in the parser; fix3 traced every reader of those locations and both token entries now run it, but a third entry path added later would need the same call. Define property values and Luau-value alternators keep their older, non-Luau reporting, which the PR discloses and which is on the base too. Six out-of-scope findings are listed in the PR's Notes and are not yet filed.
- Verification coverage: luauUnreadToken.test.ts (44 tests, each unread case compared with the official Luau parser's message and range), red/green for 77fcc6ed6 against 0a820cb1f (1 failed / 43 passed red, 44 green, restored and hash-matched), local runs on 77fcc6ed6 of TrailingCommaReassignment 101, TrailingCommaValueList 68, listCommaToken 7, MultilineAssignment1306 46, DefineUnterminated 27, invalidStatementInFunctionBody 105, typecheckSparkdown 14, tsc clean, the served VS Code workbench showing squiggles only at `@5` for both member spellings, and CI on 77fcc6ed6 all green (29 passed, 4 skipped). Rounds 1 and 2's undirected reviewers ran the changed tests on the merge base (70 and 72 failed red) and round 3's undirected reviewer read the head's Test Suite (526 files, 12,931 tests) and Typecheck (41/41) runs.
