- Agreed behavior preserved; architecture unchanged.
- Decision: All 14 findings across three rounds are accepted and fixed with red/green-verified tests, and nothing is open. The defect classes converged to edge cases of the two mechanisms rather than new root causes, round 1's correction removed the duplicate ownership implementation, and the only unreviewed change is a narrow condition that extends an existing rule to the second spelling of the same construct, verified by test, by red/green and in the served workbench, with CI green on the head. Under the coordinator's rule for this Feature, unforeseeable edge cases merge and root-cause simplifications become their own tickets: the tokenizer-level attribute lexeme is filed as a follow-up rather than widening a 42-file slice that three dependent slices wait on. Next: Accept head 77fcc6ed6 unreviewed; the writer files the six out-of-scope findings and the tokenizer attribute-lexeme simplification as tickets and sends its final report without marking the PR ready; the coordinator marks the PR ready naming this decision and merges it through the integration gate.
- Verification on the head: red/green for 77fcc6ed6 against 0a820cb1f: 1 failed / 43 passed red, 44 passed green, worktree restored and hash-matched; luauUnreadToken 44, TrailingCommaReassignment 101, TrailingCommaValueList 68, listCommaToken 7, MultilineAssignment1306 46, DefineUnterminated 27, invalidStatementInFunctionBody 105, typecheckSparkdown 14 passing on 77fcc6ed6; tsc --noEmit -p packages/sparkdown clean; served VS Code workbench on 77fcc6ed6: both define-member spellings show Luau's two errors at @5 and nothing at the =, story line after the define plain (screenshot inspected by the writer); CI on 77fcc6ed6: 29 checks passed, 4 skipped, none failed or pending.
